DIVERGENCE: spec §5.8 says `1.foo` is the selector tokens `1 . foo` (would give 'cannot access field on this type', as `x.foo` does), but the lexer greedily takes `1.` as a trailing-dot float, so `1.foo` actually fails with 'expected ; or }'. Decide spec vs impl: explorations/spec-todo.md (float-digit-dot-selector).
